hey there and welcome to inside the  Oscars I'm Rachel Smith and today we are  taking you into the most exclusive place  in Hollywood the Oscars Green Room on  Oscar night no cameras are allowed but  today we're gonna take you inside for an  exclusive look and where Hollywood's  biggest stars hang out before they take  the stage the green room is a space  right off of the stage for presenters  performers and nominees somewhere where  they can go out of prying eyes there's  no press allowed in there during the  show so it's kind of a nice little haven  away from the hustle and bustle of being  on the red carpet it's to put people in  the right frame of mind to go out and do  the job that they're there to do and I  think the stars love it because once  they've spent all day getting ready for  the show they've done countless  interviews they step into the green room  and relax before they have to go and sit  in their seat for the star of the show  or walk onstage to present an award it's  designed by Architectural Digest  Margaret Russell the editor of AD called  me up and asked if I would like to do  the green room and it felt like just  exactly the right project traditionally  the green room has been a very complete  design ours is more open-ended in that  people will be able to personalize it a  little bit there's an entry there's a  living room there's a bar and then  there's this garden in the back is  actually five at the campus transitional  buffet area the garden in the back  hopefully will be a bit of a surprise  it's not something that's expected and  and the trick is it is with many of  these these rooms is it just feel like  you're in this very protected wonderful  green room so these were just some early  research images about one of the  features that I think is going to be  most unique is what we're calling a  media wall you can see there's three  sizes and we can use it as individual  shots that show people arriving or show  people winning but it can also be used  for show graphics or for instance if  we're looking at one  particular category at home we can show  that as well so it's really going to be  an exciting element you want to create a  place where people are comfortable and  you want to create a place where there's  this sense of community so it's an  interesting design challenge so other  thing that stars themselves being  allowed in the green room there are very  few people that you get to go in there  what's nice is you get to see the stars  let the guard down they can be  themselves they can chill out we want  them to enjoy themselves and have a good  Oscar experience last year we had a  Twitter mirror in the green room and it  was a great opportunity for the nominees  presenters performers that were in the  green room to take pictures of  themselves and send to their fans always  fell down I'm here in the green room at  the Oscars and we're doing it again this  year so check it out on Oscar Sunday to  make sure you don't miss any of the vine  that seems action on Oscar Sunday  check out the Oscar buzz page on Oscar  com
 

